    fix(follower): never execute a sibling on the same parent as this node's build
    
    The own-block reuse found a kept build by the payload's parent, number and --
    under deferred execution -- the parent's result, which every sibling on that
    parent shares, and the sealed header takes the payload's beneficiary,
    timestamp, randao, gas limit and base fee, so two blocks with equal
    transactions paired. In loop157 W node4, catching up, had built its own empty
    block 183 on the parent of node2's empty block 183: it handed node2's block to
    its engine as its own build, filed its build's state root under node2's hash,
    and refused block 184.
    
    The reuse now also requires the build to execute as the sealed block: the
    beneficiary, timestamp, randao, gas limit, base fee, beacon root,
    transactions root and rewards equal. The seal changes only the view in the
    extra data, so this node's own blocks always pass.

